<title>USA: DynCorp joint venture wins $63 mln contract.</title>
<headline>DynCorp joint venture wins $63 mln contract.</headline>
<dateline>RESTON, Va. 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>High technology services company DynCorp said on Monday its joint venture, TESCO, won a four-year $63 million contract with the U.S. Army Test and Experimentation Command in Texas.</p>
<p>TESCO, which was an incumbent contractor with the U.S. Army over the past three and a half years, is a joint venture among employee-owned DynCorp, EWA Services Inc and COMARCO.</p>
<p>It would provide a range of operational testing and experimentation support, DynCorp said in a statement.</p>
<p>DynCorp said it expected to realize total revenues of $41 million from contract.</p>
<p>-- New York newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
</text>
